      "role": "user",
      "content": "My client's main argument is that these disruptions felt less like \"standard business risk\" and more like a complete breakdown of order—unpredictable, almost like everything was purposefully being sabotaged or messed with by some external, irrational force. In a legal sense, can we actually argue that the \"chaotic\" nature of the disruption qualifies, or does the law require a more concrete, quantifiable event?",
